    <statement><p>Write a triple integral including limits of integration
that gives the volume of the cap of the solid sphere
<m>x^2+y^2+z^2\le 25</m> cut off by the plane
<m>z=3</m> and restricted to the first octant.
(In your integral, use theta, rho, and phi for <m>\theta</m>,
<m>\rho</m> and <m>\phi</m>, as needed.)</p>
<p>What coordinates are you using?  <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><em>(Enter <alert>cartesian</alert>, <alert>cylindrical</alert>,
or <alert>spherical</alert>.)</em></p>
<p>With
<m>a =</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/>,
<m>b =</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/>,</p>
<p><m>c =</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/>,
<m>d =</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/>,</p>
<p><m>e =</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0006"/>, and
<m>f =</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0007"/>,</p>
<p>Volume = <m>\int_a^b\int_c^d\int_e^f</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0008"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0009"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0010"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0011"/></p>
</statement>
