    <solution><me>V = \int_0^{\pi/2}\int_0^{4}\int_{3}^{\sqrt{25 - r^2}} r\,dz\,dr\,d\theta.</me>




In cartesian, we get
<me>V = \int_0^{4}\int_0^{\sqrt{16 - x^2}}\int_{3}^{\sqrt{25-x^2-y^2}}1\,dz\,dy\,dx,</me>
and in spherical,
<me>V = \int_0^{\pi/2}\int_0^{\arccos(3/\sqrt{25})}\int_{3/\cos\phi}^{\sqrt{25}} \rho^2\,\sin\phi\,d\rho\,d\phi\,d\theta.</me>



</solution>
